{"ts":"2026-07-21T12:46:02.776Z","type":"finding","frontier":"priority-surplus-remove-authoritative-placement-fence-main","claim":"inherited from operation-ledger-quorum-authoritative-release: The real RebalanceCoordinator admission path deterministically reproduces the systemic stale-read-model lock: cache-local services rows engage operation_ledger_quorum_concentrated and current source never consults the services owner, so a complete owner observation proving three voters on three nodes cannot release the final dependent sql_write_operations ADD. The discriminator also pins the required consistency contract: owner-local or owner-RPC complete spread may release; concentrated, incomplete, unavailable, malformed, SQL-projection, or any second-ledger unspread evidence must hold; a local no-hold path performs no authority read.","kind":"inherited-rulesout","evidence":"test/convergence/dt6-operation-ledger-quorum-authoritative-release.test.js","rulesOut":"quorum arithmetic, cure typing, self-move serialization, operation budgets, host scheduling, and a missing physical ledger spread","verification":null,"regressionClassification":null,"scopePressureClassification":null}
{"ts":"2026-07-21T12:46:02.776Z","type":"finding","frontier":"priority-surplus-remove-authoritative-placement-fence-main","claim":"inherited from operation-ledger-quorum-authoritative-release: The one permitted post-fix full run is measuring red on a distinct owner boundary. control_plane_publications-p1 first reached the intended three-replica spread (ADD r4/r5; REMOVE r2/r3 complete by 12:31:20). After leadership moved to r5/node-1 at 12:31:22, that new leader planned a standalone REMOVE of r1 from a stale local superset (activeCount=4, distinct=2, spread gap open) even though canonical physical placement was already r1/r4/r5 at target and spread. The remove completed at 12:31:30, regressing actual placement to two ready replicas; meanwhile the leader's stale cache later claimed five replicas/distinct three and kept proposing removal of the already-removed r1, so no deficit ADD repaired the canonical gap. Schema admission observed priority gap 1 for 87 samples and finally lost the snapshot request. Host scheduling stayed within budget and no node exited.","kind":"inherited-rulesout","evidence":"test-output/reports/movielens-lagrange-service-affinity-live-2026-07-21T12-36-14-313Z.report.json","rulesOut":"Do not reopen operation-ledger owner-release logic, widen admission timeouts, blame host CPU, or treat the final admin timeout as first cause. The next lever is generic destructive priority-REMOVE authority/fencing across leader handoff: cache unions that are conservative for ADD are unsafe for DELETE.","verification":null,"regressionClassification":null,"scopePressureClassification":null}
{"ts":"2026-07-21T12:56:16.034Z","type":"quest-declared","sealed":{"doneWhen":{"probe":"scenario-harness","args":{"scenario":"movielens-lagrange-service-affinity-live","consecutive":1,"metric":"priority"}},"frontierMetrics":[{"probe":"scenario-harness","args":{"scenario":"movielens-lagrange-service-affinity-live","metric":"priority"}}],"authoringContractVersion":1,"statement":"For every priority control-plane partition, a non-failed standalone REMOVE is persisted only when strict services-owner evidence proves the exact source is a current active voter, voter count exceeds the policy target, and post-remove count and diversity are monotonic-safe. Unavailable or mismatched evidence defers, so leader handoff cannot turn stale superset rows into over-removal and MovieLens retains three spread control_plane_publications voters.","class":"product","constraints":[{"id":"source-change-subagent-verification","statement":"If this Quest changes source code, spawn a subagent verifier before audit and git handoff, then record a Solver finding with evidence subagent:<id>."},{"id":"destructive-boundary-only","statement":"Fence only non-failed standalone REMOVE intents for priority control-plane partitions at canonical coordinator creation. Do not change planner precedence, target selection, ADD or REPLACE behavior, failed-replica cleanup, workflow dispatch/recovery, quorum floors, budgets, or membership-publication semantics."},{"id":"strict-owner-fail-closed","statement":"Use the existing services-owner read with OWNER_RPC_REQUIRED and no SQL, cache, or follower fallback. Only a successful owner_rpc_lane observation with complete, non-conflicting replica identity may authorize deletion; unavailable, malformed, empty, duplicate, source-missing, or non-owner evidence must defer without persisting an operation."},{"id":"monotonic-removal-proof","statement":"Authoritative evidence must prove the named source is a current active voter, current active-voter count is strictly above the policy target, projected post-remove voter count remains at least target, and projected distinct-node count does not fall below the pre-remove distinct-node count. This is a compare-at-commit fence, not a second planner."},{"id":"bounded-read-surface","statement":"Perform no new authority read for non-priority entities, ADD, REPLACE, or failed-replica REMOVE. An applicable priority surplus REMOVE performs one finite services-owner observation and reuses existing policy resolution; add no timer, retry loop, cache, worker, or new eventual-consistency surface."},{"id":"witness-order-red-on-revert","statement":"Before changing source, reproduce through createOperation the exact leadership-handoff order: canonical owner rows settle at r1/r4/r5 on three nodes while the new leader plans REMOVE r1 from a stale four-row local superset. Current source persists the remove; fixed source defers it. Also cover a genuine four-voter surplus removal, duplicate/malformed rows, owner unavailability, source absence, diversity loss, failed cleanup, non-priority, and no-read paths, with red-on-revert evidence."},{"id":"live-validation-last","statement":"After deterministic, focused, model, static, and independent proof, run the unchanged five-node formation probe once and at most one full MovieLens scenario on final bytes. Preserve any red evidence and do not rerun unchanged bytes."}],"frontierIds":["priority-surplus-remove-authoritative-placement-fence-main"]}}
